# Senior DevOps Engineer - Webfleet, Leipzig
URL: https://www.eurotechjobs.com/job_display/296568/Senior_DevOps_Engineer_Webfleet_Leipzig_Germany

Senior DevOps Engineer - Webfleet, Leipzig

#### As part of the team, you will:

- Design, improve, and maintain cloud-based infrastructure and platform services;
- Work with AWS and Kubernetes to operate scalable and reliable services;
- Build, maintain, and optimize CI/CD pipelines;
- Automate infrastructure and operational processes using tools such as Terraform;
- Use Java and/or Groovy to develop, maintain, and improve automation, tooling, pipelines, and platform-related services;
- Collaborate with development teams, architects, product owners, and system engineers to support reliable delivery of new features;
- Improve monitoring, logging, metrics, alerting, and operational visibility using tools such as Grafana;
- Support stability, performance, quality assurance, incident prevention, and continuous improvement;
- Help improve deployment processes, release automation, and service operations;
- Identify, prevent, and resolve potential security and operational risks;
- Contribute to code reviews, infrastructure reviews, and technical discussions.

### Who are you?

There is no single path to becoming part of Webfleet.

#### However, to be successful in this role, we imagine you bring the following:

- Solid experience as a DevOps engineer, platform engineer, cloud engineer, or similar role;
- Strong Java and/or Groovy development skills;
- Hands-on experience with AWS and Kubernetes;
- Experience with CI/CD pipelines and tools such as Jenkins;
- Experience with container technologies such as Docker;
- Experience with infrastructure as code, preferably Terraform;
- A good understanding of cloud infrastructure, service operations, automation, monitoring, and reliability;
- An interest in working closely with software engineers, architects, component owners, and system engineers;
- Strong communication skills, an analytical mindset, and a goal-oriented, quality-focused approach;
- Knowledge of PostgreSQL would be a plus;
- A willingness to learn and adopt new technologies as needed by the team;
- Fluency in English.
